DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These functions manage the relationship between a device and device driv‐
     ers.

     ddeevviiccee__pprroobbee() invokes the DEVICE_PROBE(9) method of each suitable driver
     and to find the driver with the best match for _d_e_v.  If a matching driver
     is found, _d_e_v is set to the DS_ALIVE state and zero is returned.  If _d_e_v
     is already attached to a device driver or has been disabled via
     device_disable(9), then it will not be probed and -1 is returned.

     ddeevviiccee__aattttaacchh() fully attaches a device driver to _d_e_v.  This function
     prints a description of the device and invokes the DEVICE_ATTACH(9)
     method.  If the DEVICE_ATTACH(9) method succeeds, _d_e_v is set to the
     DS_ATTACHED state and zero is returned.  If the DEVICE_ATTACH(9) method
     fails, BUS_CHILD_DETACHED(9) is called and an error value is returned.

     If the device name and unit are disabled by a hint, ddeevviiccee__aattttaacchh() dis‐
     ables the device, demotes it to the DS_NOTPRESENT state, and returns
     ENXIO.  The device retains its device name and unit and can be re-enabled
     via devctl(8).

     ddeevviiccee__pprroobbee__aanndd__aattttaacchh() is a wrapper function around ddeevviiccee__pprroobbee() and
     ddeevviiccee__aattttaacchh() that fully initialises a device.  If _d_e_v is already at‐
     tached or disabled, ddeevviiccee__pprroobbee__aanndd__aattttaacchh() leaves the device unchanged
     and returns zero.  Otherwise, ddeevviiccee__pprroobbee() is used to identify a device
     driver for _d_e_v and ddeevviiccee__aattttaacchh() finalizes attaching the driver to _d_e_v.
     Device drivers should generally use this function to initialize a device
     rather than direct calls to ddeevviiccee__pprroobbee() and ddeevviiccee__aattttaacchh().

     ddeevviiccee__ddeettaacchh() detaches the device driver from _d_e_v.  This function in‐
     vokes the DEVICE_DETACH(9) method to tear down device driver state for
     _d_e_v.  If the method fails, its error value is returned and _d_e_v remains
     attached.  If the method succeeds, otherwise, BUS_CHILD_DETACHED(9) is
     called, the device is set to the DS_NOTPRESENT state, and zero is re‐
     turned.  If a device is busy, ddeevviiccee__ddeettaacchh() fails with EBUSY and leav‐
     ing _d_e_v unchanged.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     Zero is returned on success, otherwise an appropriate error is returned.
     In addition, ddeevviiccee__pprroobbee() returns -1 if _d_e_v is disabled or already at‐
     tached.

